  {
   "metadata": {},
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "source": [
    "## 7. Create a retention list and save the pipeline\n",
    "\n",
    "A probability threshold should match the team's offer budget. Here, customers at or above 0.60 are given high priority. The saved pipeline includes preprocessing and the model, so it can score new raw customer data consistently.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Business recommendations\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Contact high-probability customers first.\n",
    "2. Use the driver analysis to tailor offers and service interventions.\n",
    "3. Measure whether outreach reduces churn, then retrain periodically with fresh data.\n",
    "4. Tune the outreach threshold based on offer cost and customer lifetime value."
   ],
   "id": "902d87b373db18e9"
  },
  {
   "metadata": {},
   "cell_type": "code",
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null,
   "source": [
    "feature_names = best_pipeline.named_steps[\"preprocessor\"].get_feature_names_out()\n",
    "fitted_model = best_pipeline.named_steps[\"model\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "if best_model_name == \"Logistic Regression\":\n",
    "    importance = pd.DataFrame({\"feature\": feature_names, \"effect_on_churn\": fitted_model.coef_[0]})\n",
    "    importance[\"absolute_effect\"] = importance[\"effect_on_churn\"].abs()\n",
    "    top_features = importance.nlargest(15, \"absolute_effect\").sort_values(\"effect_on_churn\")\n",
    "    value_column, title = \"effect_on_churn\", \"Top Logistic Regression Effects on Churn\"\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    importance = pd.DataFrame({\"feature\": feature_names, \"importance\": fitted_model.feature_importances_})\n",
    "    top_features = importance.nlargest(15, \"importance\").sort_values(\"importance\")\n",
    "    value_column, title = \"importance\", \"Top Random Forest Feature Importances\"\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 7))\n",
    "plt.barh(top_features[\"feature\"], top_features[value_column], color=\"#2a9d8f\")\n",
    "plt.title(title)\n",
    "plt.xlabel(value_column.replace(\"_\", \" \").title())\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "top_features"
   ],
   "id": "d1547afe772d42e"
  },
  {
   "metadata": {},
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "source": [
    "## 6. Explain churn drivers\n",
    "\n",
    "The chart highlights the most influential transformed features. For Logistic Regression, positive values raise churn likelihood and negative values reduce it. For Random Forest, values are relative importance scores, not direction of effect."
   ],
   "id": "bf8a35c1abc1cf51"
  },
  {
   "metadata": {},
   "cell_type": "code",
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null,
   "source": [
    "best_model_name = results_df.index[0]\n",
    "best_pipeline = fitted_pipelines[best_model_name]\n",
    "test_probabilities = best_pipeline.predict_proba(X_test)[:, 1]\n",
    "test_predictions = (test_probabilities >= 0.50).astype(int)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Selected model: {best_model_name}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Test ROC-AUC: {roc_auc_score(y_test, test_probabilities):.3f}\")\n",
    "print(classification_report(y_test, test_predictions, target_names=[\"No Churn\", \"Churn\"]))\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(13, 5))\n",
    "ConfusionMatrixDisplay(confusion_matrix(y_test, test_predictions), display_labels=[\"No Churn\", \"Churn\"]).plot(ax=axes[0], cmap=\"Blues\", colorbar=False)\n",
    "axes[0].set_title(\"Confusion Matrix\")\n",
    "RocCurveDisplay.from_predictions(y_test, test_probabilities, ax=axes[1])\n",
    "axes[1].set_title(\"ROC Curve\")\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ],
   "id": "d6a50d91059600e4"
  },
  {
   "metadata": {},
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "source": [
    "## 5. Evaluate the selected model\n",
    "\n",
    "We now evaluate the model with the best ROC-AUC on customers it never saw during training. Alongside ROC-AUC, the classification report shows precision, recall, and F1-score. For retention teams, churn recall is useful because it measures how many truly at-risk customers are identified."
   ],
   "id": "d7f7e33319cea51a"
  },
  {
   "metadata": {},
   "cell_type": "code",
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null,
   "source": [
    "numeric_transformer = Pipeline([\n",
    "    (\"imputer\", SimpleImputer(strategy=\"median\")),\n",
    "    (\"scaler\", StandardScaler())\n",
    "])\n",
    "categorical_transformer = Pipeline([\n",
    "    (\"imputer\", SimpleImputer(strategy=\"most_frequent\")),\n",
    "    (\"onehot\", OneHotEncoder(handle_unknown=\"ignore\"))\n",
    "])\n",
    "\n",
    "preprocessor = ColumnTransformer([\n",
    "    (\"num\", numeric_transformer, numeric_features),\n",
    "    (\"cat\", categorical_transformer, categorical_features)\n",
    "])\n",
    "\n",
    "models = {\n",
    "    \"Logistic Regression\": LogisticRegression(max_iter=2000, class_weight=\"balanced\", random_state=RANDOM_STATE),\n",
    "    \"Random Forest\": RandomForestClassifier(\n",
    "        n_estimators=400, min_samples_leaf=3, class_weight=\"balanced\",\n",
    "        random_state=RANDOM_STATE, n_jobs=-1\n",
    "    )\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "fitted_pipelines, results = {}, {}\n",
    "for name, model in models.items():\n",
    "    pipeline = Pipeline([(\"preprocessor\", preprocessor), (\"model\", model)])\n",
    "    pipeline.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
    "    probabilities = pipeline.predict_proba(X_test)[:, 1]\n",
    "    results[name] = roc_auc_score(y_test, probabilities)\n",
    "    fitted_pipelines[name] = pipeline\n",
    "\n",
    "results_df = pd.DataFrame.from_dict(results, orient=\"index\", columns=[\"Test ROC-AUC\"]).sort_values(\"Test ROC-AUC\", ascending=False)\n",
    "results_df.style.format(\"{:.3f}\")"
   ],
   "id": "9c228142cc997c89"
  },
  {
   "metadata": {},
